# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/

# public/ is generated from art_src/ by `npm run art`, but it is committed
# anyway, because it is what gets deployed.
#
# Building it in CI instead would mean installing Python, Pillow and ffmpeg
# there, and a keying bug would take the site down rather than merely looking
# wrong on somebody's machine. Committing the output costs some binary churn
# whenever art is re-rolled and means the thing deployed is exactly the thing
# that was played.

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment overrides
*.local
.env
.env.*

# Python bytecode from the art tooling.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# art_src/ is raw material, not game assets, and is kept out of the repository.
#
# It holds untouched generator output -- 1024px JPEGs, several megabytes each --
# and the original audio downloads exactly as they came off Pixabay. public/ holds
# what the game actually loads, and that is tracked.
#
# Two reasons. It is heavy: every re-roll of a sprite adds another 7MB to the
# history for good, and none of it is what anybody clones the repository to get.
# And the audio in it is the untouched downloads, which is nearer to
# redistributing the sounds as sounds than shipping a game that plays them.
#
# Nothing is lost. Every sound is credited by uploader and Pixabay id in
# CREDITS.md and can be fetched again; every picture has its prompt in
# ART_PROMPTS.md. The files stay on disk, so `npm run art` still works here.
art_src/

# Sweep output is a record of a run, not source.
sweep-results/
